function AboutPage() {
  return (
    <div className="page">
      <div className="about-hero">
        <div>
          <div className="section-label-dark">About</div>
          <h1 className="section-heading-dark" style={{fontSize:"clamp(3rem,8vw,6rem)"}}>
            BREANNA<br/><span className="italic">LEE MARSH</span>
          </h1>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div className="about-content">
        <div className="about-img-wrap">
          <img
            src="data:image/jpeg;base64,"
            alt="Breanna Lee Marsh"
            style={{
              width:'100%',
              aspectRatio:'3/4',
              objectFit:'cover',
              objectPosition:'center top',
              display:'block',
            }}
          />
        </div>
        <div className="about-text">
          <div className="about-quote">
            "the true power of the FELT methodology lies in taking a backseat to the body and letting God be the navigator."
          </div>
          <div className="body-text-dark">
            <p>Breanna Lee Marsh is a mother, daughter, sister, nurturer by nature, and lover of laughter. She is also a survivor of beatings, sexual assault, emotional abuse, kidnapping, and a near-death experience.</p>
            <p>For years, she lived haunted by the weight of severe panic attacks, complex PTSD, anxiety, and depression so pervasive it reshaped the architecture of her days.</p>
            <p>She prayed daily for God to either save her or take her home.</p>
            <p>Instead, He gave her FELT.</p>
            <p>What began as her own desperate search for relief became something far larger.</p>
            <p>Because when Breanna stopped trying to fix what she felt and started listening to it instead, she discovered something the trained mind resists and the wounded body has always known: the body doesn't need to be corrected. It needs to be witnessed.</p>
            <p>The body possesses an innate intelligence that most of us have been systematically taught to override. When that intelligence is finally allowed to speak, what moves through a person is often more profound than anything a practitioner could plan or produce.</p>
            <p>What once felt like her dead end became the beginning of her healing, and the beginning for hundreds of others who have entered this work since.</p>
            <p>FELT is a body-led somatic practice rooted in nervous system and fascial work, focused on helping people reconnect with safety, regulation, and embodied truth. It emerged not from a curriculum, but from lived experience, refined through years of disciplined study as a certified yoga teacher, trauma-informed yoga therapist, transformational yoga coach, and trained life coach. Those credentials didn't create FELT. They gave Breanna the language and ethical rigour to recognise what was emerging, and to hold it with the care it requires.</p>
            <p>Today she works with a small number of people at a time. Practitioners deepening their capacity to witness their highest truth. Families learning to come back to themselves and each other. Facilitators ready to work at the edges of what transformation can look like.</p>
            <p>The work is slow by design. Intimate by necessity.</p>
            <p>Her greatest joy is simple and profound: helping people restore the connection between mind, body, and soul, and helping them rediscover the joy of being alive.</p>
            <p>She doesn't simply make room for transformation. She curates the conditions that make it inevitable, facilitating communion within the body, showing people how to allow God to enter.</p>
          </div>
          <div style={{marginTop:"3rem",padding:"2rem",border:"1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.08)",background:"var(--dark)"}}>
            <div className="section-label-dark" style={{marginBottom:"1rem"}}>The FELT Methodology</div>
            <div className="body-text-dark">
              <p><strong style={{color:"var(--white)",fontWeight:500}}>The Access</strong> — Participatory embodied awareness through body-led floor work designed to cultivate felt awareness and restore access to the body's intelligence by deepening relationship with the nervous system, cerebrospinal fluid dynamics, fascia and muscle structures.</p>
              <p><strong style={{color:"var(--white)",fontWeight:500}}>The Integration</strong> — Receptive nervous system integration through table-based bodywork with the spine, cerebrospinal fluid dynamics, fascia, and nervous system organization.</p>
              <p><strong style={{color:"var(--white)",fontWeight:500}}>The Practice</strong> — Body-led movement and experiential self-practice deepening embodiment, discernment, and sustainable relationship with the body.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  );
}

